1. URL (Uniform Resource Locator): A web address embedded within the body or links of an email.
Security filters scan these to ensure they do not point to known malicious or credential-harvesting websites.

2. Domain: The core web identity (e.g., example.com) found in email addresses and URLs.
Security systems evaluate domain age, reputation, and typosquatting safety (e.g., checking if examp1e.com is trying to mimic example.com).

3. Attachment: Any file (like a PDF, Word document, or ZIP file) appended to the email. 
Because attachments can carry malware, they are heavily scanned by email gateways.
